<title>CANADA: Canada dollar weakens on U.S. inflation fears.</title>
<headline>Canada dollar weakens on U.S. inflation fears.</headline>
<text>
<p>FORECAST RANGE   1.3940/1.3990	    ASIAN CLOSE     1.3964</p>
<p>RESISTANCE 1.3740   SUPPORT 1.3440	HI 1.3970   LO  1.3962</p>
<p>CANADA OPEN  1.3963/68    HI 1.3992     EUROPE OPEN     1.3964</p>
<p>PREV CLOSE   1.3965/70    LO 1.3954     HI 1.3972   LO  1.3962</p>
<p>----------------------MARKET COMMENT--------------------------</p>
<p>* Canada's dollar weakened slightly in light midday trading to C$1.3972 (US$0.7157) on Wednesday as markets reacted to renewed fears of creeping U.S. inflation, traders said. * They said U.S. data showing a stronger than expected surge in industrial production in March triggered broad-based Canada-selling and a late-morning push to C$1.3990 (US$0.7147).</p>
</text>
